Corresponding source: pinned archives in upstream.json, upstream nrsc5 codec
patch, wasm/nrsc5/wrapper.c, prepare.py, CMakeLists.txt, build.sh and build.mjs
in the BrowSDR repository. The browser adapter replaces native device/session
plumbing with a synchronous FM IQ pipe. Its generated output adapter decodes only
the selected audio program and omits unused enhanced-stream packet buffers.
RF, FEC and codec algorithms are unchanged.
No native SDR drivers, sockets, filesystem input, or native audio output is used.
